      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. It verifies that `withOverrides()` computes the intersection of included property sets, and the merged result is a new distinct `Value` different from both inputs. I'll improve understandability by using meaningful variable names and adding clarifying comments.Now I'll compile-check the generated test.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version replaces cryptic auto-generated variable names (`linkedHashSet0`, `jsonIncludeProperties_Value0`, etc.) with descriptive names (`propertiesInOverride`, `overrideValue`, `baseValue`, `mergedValue`) and adds a Javadoc comment explaining the test's intent — that `withOverrides()` computes the intersection of disjoint property sets, yielding an empty result distinct from both inputs."
